Hi,

During the development of rpy2 few 64bit-specific issues slipped in,
causing sudden terminations of the python process (read "segfault").
Yaroslav Halchenko (from the PyMVPA project/) brought the problems to
my attention last week, and they were finally fixed.

I am heading for rpy-2.1.0-alpha3 (planned to be the last alpha), but
before that I would appreciate if 64bit users out there, and OS X 10.6
users,
could confirm that seems to be working.

Thanks,


Laurent

PS: There are still minor issues with the new NA types. Nothing to be
bothered about until alpha 3.

